# Project Calibration Governance

Applies when running `/calibrate`, invoking **Master Agent**, or using the `project-calibration` skill.

## Scope

Calibration adjusts **Cursor configuration only**:

- `AGENTS.md`
- `.cursor/agents/**`
- `.cursor/commands/**`
- `.cursor/rules/project-stack.mdc` (generated)
- `.cursor/calibration/**` (generated artifacts)

## Never during calibration

- Modify application source (`src/`, `app/`, `lib/`, `services/`, etc.)
- Delete host-created `.cursor/**` files
- Read or commit `.env`, secrets, or credentials
- Copy secret **values** into `stack-profile.json` (evidence = paths and field names only)
- Replace `tech-stack.mdc` (add `project-stack.mdc` only)
- Overwrite `AGENTS.local.md` or `settings.local.json`

## Required workflow

1. **Discover** — write `.cursor/calibration/stack-profile.json` with evidence
2. **Report** — write `.cursor/calibration/manifest.md` (dry-run default)
3. **Apply** — write only after user confirms manifest or `--apply` flag

## Preserve host customizations

Files not shipped by `cursor-agents` or clearly host-authored must appear under **Skip** in the manifest. When in doubt, skip.

## Name collisions

See `.cursor/references/name-collision-playbook.md`.

| Collision type | Manifest section | Apply behavior |
|----------------|------------------|----------------|
| Same **path** as package asset | **Skip (preserve host)** | Never overwrite |
| Same frontmatter **`name:`**, different paths | **Conflict (manual resolution)** | Ask user; never auto-rename or delete |
| Host-only custom file | **Skip** | Preserve |

Never auto-resolve **Conflict** during Apply.

## Generated artifacts (commit to git)

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `.cursor/rules/project-stack.mdc` | Repo-specific stack (`alwaysApply: true`) |
| `.cursor/calibration/stack-profile.json` | Machine-readable profile + evidence |
| `.cursor/calibration/manifest.md` | Optional audit trail of last calibration |

## Force mode

`--force` may overwrite **only** previously generated calibration artifacts listed above and patches explicitly listed in the manifest. It must not delete custom rules.
